  <section class="py-16 px-6 lg:px-24 bg-japandi-sand/25 border-y border-japandi-clay/30">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto space-y-12">
      
      <!-- Step 4 H2 #1: Bleeding Gums, Swollen Gums & Early Gingivitis -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-4xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium tracking-tight">
          Bleeding Gums &amp; Swollen Gums: Early Signs of Gum Disease
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          Gums and surrounding bone form the foundation that keeps your natural teeth anchored in your jaw. When bacterial plaque and mineralized tartar (calculus) accumulate along and below the gum margin, bacteria trigger chronic inflammation.
        </p>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          In its early stage, known as <strong>gingivitis</strong>, gums become swollen, tender, and bleed easily during brushing or flossing. Because gingivitis is confined to the soft tissues and has not yet damaged the underlying bone, early gum disease (gingivitis) can usually be reversed with treatment and good home care.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 4 H2 #2: Gum Disease and Pyorrhea (Periodontitis) -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium tracking-tight">
          Understanding Gum Disease and Pyorrhea (Periodontitis)
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          If gingivitis is left unaddressed, bacteria migrate deeper beneath the gumline, triggering an aggressive inflammatory response. This advanced condition, commonly known as <strong>pyorrhea</strong> or <strong>periodontitis</strong>, creates infected periodontal pockets. The bacterial toxins gradually dissolve the alveolar bone and periodontal connective fibers that secure the tooth root. Left untreated, progressive bone destruction leads to gum recession, chronic bad breath, tooth mobility, and eventual tooth loss.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 4 H2 #3: Modern Laser Gum Treatment in Hennur -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium tracking-tight">
          Modern Laser Gum Treatment in Hennur
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          At Aureva Dental, we utilize modern dental laser therapy for targeted, comfortable decontamination of periodontal pockets. The focused laser energy helps reduce bacteria in gum pockets and vaporizes infected pocket lining while leaving healthy connective tissue unharmed. Because the laser simultaneously seals microscopic blood vessels, treatment involves minimal bleeding, no scalpels or surgical incisions, no sutures, and significantly faster recovery times compared to conventional periodontal surgery.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 4 H2 #4: How a Periodontist Plans Treatment -->
      <div class="space-y-4">
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium tracking-tight">
          How a Periodontist Plans Treatment
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          Effective periodontal therapy requires systematic diagnosis rather than guesswork. For patients presenting with moderate to advanced periodontitis, our resident dental surgeons work alongside experienced visiting periodontists (gum specialists) on call. Periodontist treatment planning follows a structured protocol:
        </p>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light pt-2">
          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">1. Periodontal Pocket Charting &amp; Digital RVG Bone Assessment</h4>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
              We measure pocket depths around every individual tooth using a calibrated periodontal probe and acquire low-radiation digital RVG radiographs to map horizontal and vertical bone loss accurately.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">2. Deep Periodontal Scaling &amp; Root Planing</h4>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
              Ultrasonic instruments meticulously remove subgingival calculus and bacterial colonies from root surfaces. Root planing then smooths the microscopic root contours, enabling the gum tissue to readapt and heal tightly around the tooth.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">3. Laser Pocket Decontamination &amp; Maintenance Protocol</h4>
            <p class="leading-relaxed">
              Deep pockets receive targeted laser therapy to sterilize subgingival flora, followed by a personalized 3-month or 6-month periodontal maintenance schedule to ensure long-term clinical stability.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Step 4 H2 #5: Gum Treatment Cost in Hennur Table Section -->
      <div id="pricing" class="space-y-6 pt-6 border-t border-japandi-clay/30">
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-japandi-moss">Transparent Pricing</span>
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-3xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">
            Gum Treatment Cost in Hennur
          </h2>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
            Straightforward pricing with complete clarity before beginning any procedure.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-japandi-clay/40 bg-japandi-sand/30">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light">
            <thead class="bg-japandi-sand/80 text-japandi-charcoal font-medium border-b border-japandi-clay/40">
              <tr>
                <th class="p-4">Periodontal Procedure</th>
                <th class="p-4">Clinical Inclusions</th>
                <th class="p-4">Published Fee (INR)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-japandi-clay/20">
              <tr>
                <td class="p-4 font-medium text-japandi-charcoal">New Patient Consultation (Incl. RVG X-ray)</td>
                <td class="p-4">Clinical periodontal examination &amp; digital radiograph</td>
                <td class="p-4 text-japandi-moss font-semibold">₹600</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-4 font-medium text-japandi-charcoal">Routine Ultrasonic Scaling and Polishing</td>
                <td class="p-4">Supragingival plaque &amp; tartar removal and airflow polishing</td>
                <td class="p-4 text-japandi-moss font-semibold">₹2,000 – ₹5,000</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-4 font-medium text-japandi-charcoal">Deep Periodontal Scaling / Root Planing</td>
                <td class="p-4">Subgingival ultrasonic debridement, root planing &amp; antiseptic irrigation</td>
                <td class="p-4 text-japandi-moss font-semibold">₹8,000 – ₹15,000</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="p-4 font-medium text-japandi-charcoal">Laser Gum Treatment</td>
                <td class="p-4">Targeted laser pocket sterilization &amp; soft-tissue decontamination</td>
                <td class="p-4 text-japandi-moss font-semibold">Price depends on the case. Consultation ₹600.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Symptoms & When to Seek Periodontal Care -->
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <h3 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-serif text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">
          When Should You Consult a Dentist for Gum Care?
        </h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light leading-relaxed">
          Gum disease is often silent in its earliest stages, which is why many patients do not seek treatment until significant bone support is compromised. We recommend booking an evaluation if you notice:
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 text-xs sm:text-sm text-japandi-earth font-light">
          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2.5">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">Common Symptoms</h4>
            <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc list-inside">
              <li>Pink toothbrush bristles or blood spitting when brushing.</li>
              <li>Puffy, tender, or purplish-red gums.</li>
              <li>Chronic unpleasant breath or bad taste in the mouth.</li>
              <li>Receding gum margins making teeth look abnormally long.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-japandi-cream/90 border border-japandi-clay/40 space-y-2.5">
            <h4 class="font-serif text-base text-japandi-charcoal font-medium">Advanced Warning Signs</h4>
            <ul class="space-y-2 list-disc list-inside">
              <li>Pus discharge or small pockets between teeth and gums.</li>
              <li>Slight loosening or mobility in adult teeth.</li>
              <li>Shifting spaces or newly developing gaps between teeth.</li>
              <li>Changes in how your upper and lower teeth meet during chewing.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
